1
00:00:00,320 --> 00:00:04,400
Is the world ending on
Friday, November 13th, 2026?

2
00:00:05,300 --> 00:00:08,020
That date comes from a real
1960 paper in the journal

3
00:00:08,020 --> 00:00:08,820
Science.

4
00:00:09,620 --> 00:00:12,680
Three researchers fitted
2,000 years of population

5
00:00:12,680 --> 00:00:14,220
estimates to one curve.

6
00:00:14,660 --> 00:00:18,200
Growth kept speeding up,
so their curve hit infinite

7
00:00:18,200 --> 00:00:20,240
people on that exact Friday.

8
00:00:21,180 --> 00:00:23,500
It was a warning,
not a prophecy.

9
00:00:24,460 --> 00:00:25,360
And it didn't hold.

10
00:00:26,160 --> 00:00:28,900
Families got smaller, and
real numbers fell behind

11
00:00:28,900 --> 00:00:29,700
the curve.
